---
// The three things an owner can do when a private car's first COE runs out, and
// when each one puts the car back into the supply pipeline. HTML only. Rules per
// LTA OneMotoring's COE renewal page (checked 5 November 2026). Ordinary private
// cars only; the ages shown assume the car was registered new.
import './coe.css';
import ToolBrand from '../ToolBrand.astro';
---

<div class="coe" data-card="figure">
  <div class="coe-head">
    <span class="coe-lbl">Three ways out of a ten-year COE</span>
    <span class="coe-sub">Private car registered new &middot; renewing is a fixed price, not a bid</span>
  </div>

  <div class="coe-body">
    <div class="coe-paths" role="list">
      <div class="coe-start">At about age 10, the first COE expires. The owner chooses:</div>
      <div class="coe-path" role="listitem">
        <div class="ch"><b>Let the car go</b><span>Deregister: scrap or export</span></div>
        <div class="nx">The deregistration feeds <b>new COE supply</b> over the following year. Cars reaching
        ten now get a PARF rebate of 50% of the ARF they paid.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="coe-path" role="listitem">
        <div class="ch"><b>Renew for 5 years</b><span>Pay 50% of the PQP</span></div>
        <div class="nx">Allowed <b>once only</b>. At about 15 the car must be deregistered, so it reaches
        the pipeline five years later.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="coe-path" role="listitem">
        <div class="ch"><b>Renew for 10 years</b><span>Pay 100% of the PQP</span></div>
        <div class="nx">Can be <b>repeated</b> at about 20, 30 and beyond. Each renewal holds the car out
        of the pipeline for another ten years.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="coe-notes">
    <p>PQP, the Prevailing Quota Premium, is the average COE price of the previous three months with
    bidding. A renewed car gets no PARF rebate when it is finally deregistered. Renewing before the expiry month forfeits the unused days.
    A late renewal is possible up to a month after expiry, with a fee. Source: LTA OneMotoring, COE renewal
    and PARF rebate pages, checked 5 November 2026. Company cars with a statutory lifespan are excluded.</p>
    <ToolBrand />
  </div>
</div>
